#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-21|author=w:Oliver Burkeman| volume=189| issue=2| page=27| magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly| title=The tao of tech|url=http://www.guardian.co.uk/technology/2013/may/10/conscious-computing-twitter-facebook-google| passage=The dirty secret of the internet is that all this distraction and interruption is immensely profitable. Web companies like to boast about&nbsp;[&hellip;], or offering services that let you{{...}}"share the things you love with the world" and so on. But the '''real''' way to build a successful online business is to be better than your rivals at undermining people's control of their own attention.}}
